WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.490
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.257
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:16.819
Unit twenty-five: Review: Growing as a Learner. Today you will reflect on learning with the present perfect continuous.

4
00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:19.759
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.910
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.461
Learner.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.403
Learner means a person who is learning.

8
00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:30.668
I'm a curious learner.

9
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:33.611
Your turn. Say: Learner.

10
00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:37.201
Learner.

11
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.137
Strategy.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.382
Strategy means a plan to reach a goal.

13
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:45.517
My strategy is to review every night.

14
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:48.583
Your turn. Say: Strategy.

15
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:52.469
Strategy.

16
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:54.125
Mistake.

17
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:57.221
Mistake means something done wrong.

18
00:00:57.817 --> 00:00:59.909
Every mistake teaches me something.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.832
Your turn. Say: Mistake.

20
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:06.772
Mistake.

21
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:08.425
Practice.

22
00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:12.670
Practice means doing something again and again to improve.

23
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:15.132
Practice makes progress.

24
00:01:15.717 --> 00:01:18.462
Your turn. Say: Practice.

25
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.278
Practice.

26
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:24.029
Feedback.

27
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.655
Feedback means comments about how well you did.

28
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.308
I ask my teacher for feedback.

29
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:33.383
Your turn. Say: Feedback.

30
00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:37.107
Feedback.

31
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:38.561
Goal.

32
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.724
Goal means something you want to achieve.

33
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:44.560
My goal is to speak English fluently.

34
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.686
Your turn. Say: Goal.

35
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:51.256
Goal.

36
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:53.041
Improve.

37
00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.933
Improve means to get better.

38
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.642
My writing has improved a lot.

39
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.705
Your turn. Say: Improve.

40
00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:05.591
Improve.

41
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.398
Motivation.

42
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:11.474
Motivation means the reason or energy to keep going.

43
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:14.141
My dream job is my motivation.

44
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.576
Your turn. Say: Motivation.

45
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:21.632
Motivation.

46
00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:26.026
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:30.081
Visal, we've finished Book Three! How do you feel?

48
00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.975
Proud! I have been practising every day.

49
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:37.350
What strategy works best for you?

50
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.075
Learning from my mistakes and asking for feedback.

51
00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:44.486
And your next goal?

52
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:52.241
B two! I have been reading English stories, and my motivation is high.

53
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.098
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.354
Grammar focus: Present perfect continuous.

55
00:02:59.654 --> 00:03:00.934
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.742
I have been practising every day.

57
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.870
She has been reading English stories.

58
00:03:07.783 --> 00:03:09.678
We have been learning for three years.

59
00:03:10.633 --> 00:03:14.862
Use it for actions that started in the past and are still continuing now.

60
00:03:15.617 --> 00:03:19.024
Be careful! Don't say: I have been practise every day.

61
00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.721
Say: I have been practising every day.

62
00:03:24.021 --> 00:03:25.962
After 'have been', use the -ing form.

63
00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.268
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.404
My Learning Journey.

65
00:03:31.704 --> 00:03:33.750
A good learner uses a strategy.

66
00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:38.543
A good learner learns from every mistake and asks for feedback.

67
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:42.346
I have been practising English every day this year.

68
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:46.146
With practice and motivation, I can reach my goal.

69
00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:49.620
I will keep improving, step by step.

70
00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:54.863
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:55.717 --> 00:03:57.496
I have been blank every day.

72
00:03:57.796 --> 00:04:01.623
A, practising. B, practise. C, practised.

73
00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.189
The answer is A: practising.

74
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.117
Something done wrong is a blank.

75
00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:14.140
A, mistake. B, goal. C, strategy.

76
00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.723
The answer is A: mistake.

77
00:04:20.883 --> 00:04:22.987
Comments about how well you did are blank.

78
00:04:23.287 --> 00:04:27.336
A, feedback. B, motivation. C, practice.

79
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.085
The answer is A: feedback.

80
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.626
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:38.483 --> 00:04:40.831
What learning strategy works best for you?

82
00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:50.966
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:51.266 --> 00:04:59.561
Speaking every day works best for me. I have been talking with my classmates in English, and my confidence has grown a lot.

84
00:04:59.861 --> 00:05:01.675
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:02.583 --> 00:05:07.337
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect continuous.

86
00:05:07.637 --> 00:05:13.195
Today's value is growth mindset. Mistakes help you grow. Keep learning, step by step.

87
00:05:13.495 --> 00:05:19.273
Congratulations! You have finished Online B one, Book three. See you in Online B two!

88
00:05:19.573 --> 00:05:22.213
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

